WEBVTT

00:06.557 --> 00:08.347
[SITARA] But this must be
the moment

00:08.477 --> 00:09.597
I've been waiting for.

00:09.727 --> 00:11.227
[gasps] How so?

00:11.347 --> 00:13.437
What could we hope
to accomplish?

00:13.557 --> 00:15.107
I have great knowledge.

00:15.477 --> 00:16.567
If you'll allow,

00:16.817 --> 00:19.027
I'll serve you as your
new Jada stone, Highness.

00:19.147 --> 00:22.157
Please, just lend me your power.

00:23.947 --> 00:27.707
And the two of us
can summon a fierce storm.

00:28.077 --> 00:29.747
[insects trilling]

00:33.287 --> 00:35.127
[Sitara sighs softly]

00:36.127 --> 00:38.667
What have I done?
Not only did I ignore

00:38.797 --> 00:41.177
Princess Sorghaghtani's
orders...

00:41.297 --> 00:43.467
[gasps softly] Hold on,

00:43.597 --> 00:45.177
I'm not...

00:45.307 --> 00:46.637
♪

00:47.767 --> 00:49.017
[gasps]

00:50.597 --> 00:53.227
I'm not her slave, am I?

00:55.267 --> 00:58.317
Ah, there you are. Fatima!

00:59.067 --> 01:01.657
[SITARA] Lady Töregene
and I have suffered greatly,

01:01.777 --> 01:04.157
but she's been forced
to bear her pain

01:04.277 --> 01:05.577
far longer than mine.

01:05.697 --> 01:07.157
-[SHIRA] Hey.
-Which is why...

01:07.867 --> 01:10.077
Tell this
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

01:10.197 --> 01:11.327
I've found my way

01:11.417 --> 01:13.707
into a much more
convenient position out here.

01:13.827 --> 01:16.037
Uh, is that right?

01:16.417 --> 01:18.297
Well, all the better then.

01:20.717 --> 01:22.217
[SITARA] No need to worry.

01:22.337 --> 01:25.967
I understand now.
I know what I must do.

01:27.007 --> 01:28.427
[Shira exhales]

01:30.517 --> 01:34.807
[SITARA]
So just you wait, Mongols.

01:35.227 --> 01:36.647
♪

01:39.857 --> 01:43.947
[♪ opening theme song playing]

03:19.037 --> 03:20.707
[groans] Uh?

03:20.837 --> 03:22.087
♪

03:25.877 --> 03:28.547
Uh, what's all this, Chagatai?

03:30.467 --> 03:31.887
[Ögedei groans]

03:33.007 --> 03:35.217
I offer you
my deepest apologies.

03:35.347 --> 03:37.267
[ÖGEDEI AND ILÜGE] Huh?

03:37.387 --> 03:40.307
First, I challenged
the Great Kha'an to a wager.

03:40.437 --> 03:43.517
Then I displayed the utmost
insolence by actually winning.

03:43.647 --> 03:45.067
Oh, you mean that?

03:46.147 --> 03:47.647
[ÖGEDEI] Oh...

03:47.907 --> 03:49.487
For this grave offense,

03:49.607 --> 03:50.987
I am prepared to be flogged

03:51.117 --> 03:53.037
or even to receive
a death sentence.

03:53.157 --> 03:55.077
Please do with me as you will.

03:55.697 --> 03:56.787
Hm?

03:58.037 --> 04:00.747
[chuckles] You are forgiven,
my brother.

04:00.877 --> 04:03.247
You know
I am not angered so easily.

04:04.287 --> 04:05.457
Uh?

04:07.417 --> 04:10.467
Ögedei Kha'an
has shown me his mercy!

04:10.587 --> 04:13.007
Let us all praise
his noble benevolence!

04:13.137 --> 04:15.307
[ALL] Huzzah!

04:15.637 --> 04:17.427
Huzzah!

04:17.557 --> 04:20.187
-Huh? What is all this?
- Huzzah!

04:22.687 --> 04:25.107
-Huh?
-I now take my leave.

04:29.357 --> 04:32.237
I swear,
why did Chagatai do all that?

04:32.527 --> 04:34.827
[CHINQAI] The prince put on
that performance for your sake.

04:35.327 --> 04:36.577
[ÖGEDEI] Chinqai?

04:38.117 --> 04:40.367
As one who only recently
took the throne,

04:40.497 --> 04:43.327
honor upon your name
is of the greatest importance.

04:43.457 --> 04:46.707
And what quality is prized most
among steppe tribe leaders?

04:46.837 --> 04:48.127
Benevolence?

04:48.337 --> 04:52.507
Exactly. Cruel to his foes,
and benevolent to his subjects.

04:52.637 --> 04:55.557
You've now proven yourself
to be precisely that.

04:55.677 --> 04:57.767
Well, I suppose it makes sense.

04:57.887 --> 04:59.727
But why be so dramatic?

04:59.847 --> 05:01.057
Huh?

05:02.477 --> 05:03.647
Now I understand.

05:03.767 --> 05:06.267
-[birds screeching]
-Benevolence, indeed.

05:06.647 --> 05:07.897
♪

05:08.777 --> 05:11.277
[SITARA (ADULT)] Kurultais were
held under Ögedei Kha'an

05:11.397 --> 05:14.777
to discuss matters
concerning future policies.

05:14.907 --> 05:18.787
And in the Mongol Empire,
the emperor's consorts took part

05:18.907 --> 05:20.867
in these political matters
as well.

05:21.617 --> 05:22.827
[Kirgistani grunts]

05:23.917 --> 05:25.127
Töregene?

05:25.247 --> 05:27.837
What are you doing,
attending a Kurultai?

05:27.957 --> 05:29.337
You're hardly ever at these.

05:29.457 --> 05:30.547
Am I not permitted?

05:30.667 --> 05:33.547
Some would give anything
to be here but cannot.

05:33.677 --> 05:34.837
[MÖGE] Hmph!

05:34.967 --> 05:37.007
[ÖGEDEI] Uh? [chuckles]

05:37.137 --> 05:39.177
[MÖGE] Uh? [chuckles]

05:39.307 --> 05:40.347
♪

05:42.477 --> 05:44.477
-Listen, Uqai.
-My name's Otai.

05:44.597 --> 05:46.397
Please try to remember that,
dear Father.

05:46.517 --> 05:47.437
[TEMÜGE] Mm...

05:48.397 --> 05:50.527
Today's meeting will outline
our next military campaign.

05:50.647 --> 05:53.697
Soon, we'll head eastward
and target the Jin Dynasty.

05:53.817 --> 05:54.817
[OTAI] From what I've heard,

05:55.027 --> 05:56.657
they're responsible
for abducting and killing

05:56.777 --> 05:58.327
many of our forefathers.

05:58.447 --> 06:00.947
Yes, but that's frankly
of little consequence

06:01.077 --> 06:02.117
at this point.

06:03.707 --> 06:05.497
House Tolui
has the largest army.

06:05.627 --> 06:08.167
But House Chagatai
has the Kha'an's trust.

06:08.297 --> 06:11.707
The head of House Jochi is dead
and his territory's far away.

06:11.837 --> 06:13.757
Whereas the lands of my House
of Temüge

06:13.877 --> 06:15.507
are close to the Jin's domain.

06:15.637 --> 06:16.797
Because our houses rule

06:16.927 --> 06:19.217
over quite a large number
of subjects as of now,

06:19.347 --> 06:22.347
we all want roles for ourselves
that won't incur losses.

06:22.467 --> 06:24.727
So I'm wondering
how the new Kha'an

06:24.847 --> 06:26.647
will attempt to appease
each one of us.

06:26.767 --> 06:27.977
Thoughts. Daritai?

06:28.107 --> 06:29.517
Otai, Father.

06:29.647 --> 06:31.437
[all murmuring]

06:31.567 --> 06:32.857
Yes, true.

06:34.567 --> 06:37.367
How will you handle
such an important matter,

06:37.907 --> 06:39.487
Great Kha'an?

06:43.367 --> 06:44.537
[Ögedei inhales]

06:45.827 --> 06:48.037
I wish to build a great capital.

06:48.167 --> 06:49.287
[ALL] Huh?

06:49.417 --> 06:50.547
[CHAGATAI] Uh-oh.

06:50.667 --> 06:53.087
[all gasp]

06:53.207 --> 06:54.717
A capital, huh?

06:54.837 --> 06:56.757
Indeed, a capital.

06:56.887 --> 06:59.097
We will construct a city
in the steppe.

06:59.217 --> 07:01.717
One made of permanent buildings,
rather than our tents.

07:01.847 --> 07:04.227
Ah! What are you going on about?

07:04.347 --> 07:06.477
What of the campaign
to bring down the Jin?

07:06.597 --> 07:07.937
A capital, you say?

07:08.057 --> 07:09.647
Do we all have to live there?

07:09.767 --> 07:11.937
[VASSAL 1] We Mongols
take pride in crossing mountains

07:12.067 --> 07:13.437
in pursuit of unseen lands.

07:13.567 --> 07:15.607
[VASSAL 2] Live like
settled people? Disgusting.

07:16.237 --> 07:19.657
Everyone, the Great Kha'an
hasn't finished speaking yet.

07:20.367 --> 07:23.537
[ÖGEDEI] It will be a capital,
but not one for us to live in.

07:23.657 --> 07:25.197
Workshops will be provided there

07:25.327 --> 07:27.247
for crafting weapons
and jewelry.

07:27.367 --> 07:29.287
It will also serve
as a trading post

07:29.417 --> 07:30.747
where merchants can gather.

07:30.877 --> 07:33.877
We will all continue
our nomadic lifestyles.

07:34.007 --> 07:37.467
But at times,
we will visit and spend freely.

07:37.587 --> 07:39.757
In a show of our grace
and benevolence.

07:39.887 --> 07:41.807
When word spreads
of such a place,

07:41.927 --> 07:43.597
it's sure to attract
people and goods

07:43.717 --> 07:45.017
from across the land.

07:45.137 --> 07:46.307
What say you?

07:46.677 --> 07:48.517
This doesn't make
any sense at all.

07:48.637 --> 07:50.437
[all murmuring]

07:50.557 --> 07:52.817
[exhales] Will it not work?

07:53.567 --> 07:55.647
Hmm...

07:55.777 --> 07:57.487
[TOLUI] Sounds great to me!

07:59.277 --> 08:00.697
♪

08:01.737 --> 08:05.037
It's quite a curious proposal,
and one worth doing.

08:05.157 --> 08:06.787
[chuckles] Tolui.

08:06.907 --> 08:09.037
Tell me, Great Kha'an.

08:12.667 --> 08:15.297
When will we all
discuss the matter of war?

08:15.417 --> 08:16.707
[ÖGEDEI] Uh?

08:16.837 --> 08:18.587
[Kirgistani grunts] Huh?

08:19.217 --> 08:23.637
Now the time is ripe to destroy
our sworn foes, the Jin.

08:24.637 --> 08:26.467
[TOLUI] Their formerly
vast territory has shrunk,

08:26.597 --> 08:28.557
so they're cornered
like tiny rats.

08:28.677 --> 08:31.977
And dealing the last blow
will be our Great Kha'an!

08:32.517 --> 08:33.517
[Ögedei chuckles]

08:34.517 --> 08:36.277
[TOLUI] This war will be just
like a circle hunt.

08:36.397 --> 08:39.197
Our quarry...
The Jin capital, Kaifeng.

08:39.317 --> 08:42.237
The Great Kha'an will set up
camp across the Yellow River,

08:42.367 --> 08:43.947
directly to the north of it.

08:44.077 --> 08:46.117
While the rats tremble in fear,

08:46.237 --> 08:47.827
we'll pincer them
from the south.

08:47.947 --> 08:51.497
That sounds more like hunting
deer than rats, if you ask me.

08:51.617 --> 08:53.537
Call them fawns if you prefer.

08:53.667 --> 08:56.207
Tolui, you mustn't
underestimate them.

08:56.337 --> 08:57.627
Though on the verge of collapse,

08:57.757 --> 09:00.587
the Jin vastly outnumber us
in both soldiers and subjects.

09:00.717 --> 09:01.797
[Tolui laughs]

09:01.927 --> 09:03.797
Which is why I want you
to begin attacking

09:03.927 --> 09:06.217
from the east and have
their citizens running, Uncle.

09:06.347 --> 09:07.347
[TEMÜGE] Hmm?

09:07.517 --> 09:09.227
[TOLUI] Just like you would
coax animals

09:09.347 --> 09:10.767
into a hunting circle.

09:10.887 --> 09:12.847
If we can chase the rest
of the Jin populace

09:12.977 --> 09:14.807
inside Kaifeng's walls,

09:15.057 --> 09:17.267
all those soldiers and subjects
you mentioned

09:17.397 --> 09:20.397
will be trapped in a city
that's completely closed off.

09:20.527 --> 09:22.987
After winter passes
and all their food runs out,

09:23.107 --> 09:25.617
I wonder what state
their poor town will be in.

09:25.737 --> 09:27.867
[laughs]

09:27.987 --> 09:29.327
[Chagatai clears throat]

09:29.867 --> 09:31.997
Oh, uh, as for you, brother...

09:32.117 --> 09:34.957
I think it's best if you
stay here and look after things.

09:35.077 --> 09:37.167
We should leave
our precious homeland

09:37.287 --> 09:40.417
to the one the Great Kha'an
trusts more than anyone, right?

09:40.547 --> 09:41.417
[ÖGEDEI] Hm.

09:41.547 --> 09:43.587
Well, that's fine.

09:43.717 --> 09:44.797
♪

09:46.637 --> 09:49.597
Jochi's kin will not have a part
to play here, I'm afraid.

09:49.717 --> 09:50.807
[ORDA] Huh?

09:52.307 --> 09:53.847
In exchange for this,

09:53.977 --> 09:56.727
you will be leading some of our
other campaigns to the west.

09:56.857 --> 09:58.357
[ORDA] Mm...

09:58.517 --> 10:00.277
[TOLUI] How does that sound?

10:00.397 --> 10:02.897
Are any of you unhappy
with these war plans?

10:05.607 --> 10:07.237
-[CHINQAI] Prince Tolui.
-Huh?

10:07.367 --> 10:09.827
In order to approach Kaifeng
from the south,

10:09.947 --> 10:13.247
our warriors will be forced
into Southern Song territory.

10:13.367 --> 10:15.707
And through precipitous
mountain roads at that.

10:15.827 --> 10:17.287
It won't be a problem.

10:17.417 --> 10:19.747
The Southern Song are enemies
of the Jin, too,

10:19.877 --> 10:21.547
which makes them a friend to us.

10:21.667 --> 10:24.667
Now as for
the precipitous mountains...

10:25.177 --> 10:26.927
we'll prevail.

10:31.267 --> 10:34.057
[TÖREGENE] That's everything
they discussed at the Kurultai.

10:34.557 --> 10:36.397
Thank you very much.

10:37.267 --> 10:39.977
If Tolui's plans
eventually succeed,

10:40.107 --> 10:43.317
starvation and cold will await
the people of Kaifeng.

10:43.437 --> 10:45.817
I'm confronted
with this knowledge,

10:45.947 --> 10:46.857
yet I still...

10:46.987 --> 10:48.327
-[breathes shakily]
-Sitara,

10:48.447 --> 10:50.407
do you feel unwell?
You're trembling.

10:50.527 --> 10:51.657
[Sitara gasps]

10:52.037 --> 10:54.577
[stutters] I'm all right.
My apologies.

10:55.907 --> 10:57.497
Sitara...

11:00.287 --> 11:01.627
Lady Töregene,

11:01.747 --> 11:04.757
I would prefer it
if you called me Fatima, please.

11:04.877 --> 11:06.007
Fatima?

11:06.127 --> 11:09.597
Sitara is my name
from when I was a slave.

11:10.177 --> 11:12.307
It'd be improper
for somebody of low birth

11:12.427 --> 11:14.847
to serve the
Great Kha'an's consort.

11:15.177 --> 11:16.347
[Töregene sighs]

11:17.307 --> 11:20.017
I, too, pass myself off
as a Naiman here.

11:20.147 --> 11:21.227
[SITARA] Uh?

11:21.357 --> 11:23.277
[TÖREGENE]
After marrying a Merkit man,

11:23.397 --> 11:25.487
I would naturally
call myself one as well.

11:25.607 --> 11:27.197
But there are
quite a few Mongols

11:27.317 --> 11:29.027
who don't take kindly to them.

11:29.737 --> 11:32.577
That's why I chose
to hide my past,

11:32.697 --> 11:35.327
and kept it a secret
from everyone I could.

11:35.457 --> 11:36.747
[Sitara gasps]

11:37.537 --> 11:40.417
Please keep it
a secret, too, Fatima.

11:40.707 --> 11:41.837
[SITARA] I will.

11:42.787 --> 11:45.667
She has the scent
of danger about her.

11:45.797 --> 11:48.337
So then, where do we go
from here?

11:48.467 --> 11:50.677
First, there is indeed
a power imbalance

11:50.797 --> 11:53.177
between the Great Kha'an
and Tolui family.

11:53.307 --> 11:56.477
The House of Tolui commands
the largest Mongol army.

11:56.597 --> 11:58.187
The Great Kha'an has authority.

11:58.637 --> 12:01.187
And the House of Chagatai
supports him.

12:01.307 --> 12:03.517
We must cause a rift
between them.

12:03.937 --> 12:05.397
But in order to do that,

12:05.527 --> 12:07.487
Prince Tolui's big plan

12:07.607 --> 12:09.607
will need to go off
successfully.

12:10.067 --> 12:11.117
♪

12:11.237 --> 12:12.657
[Boraqchin coughs]

12:14.827 --> 12:16.827
[MÖGE] Pardon the intrusion.

12:17.287 --> 12:18.577
[chuckles]

12:20.077 --> 12:22.247
How are you feeling, Boraqchin?

12:23.997 --> 12:25.297
Well, seeing your face

12:25.417 --> 12:26.957
has certainly
brightened my mood a little.

12:27.917 --> 12:29.427
What do you have there?

12:29.547 --> 12:30.677
This is a medical text

12:30.797 --> 12:32.677
brought here
by Quanzhen Daoists.

12:32.797 --> 12:34.097
[MÖGE] Hmm...

12:34.217 --> 12:36.307
Just through the process
of living,

12:36.427 --> 12:38.427
our bodies gradually lose
their qi,

12:38.557 --> 12:40.437
which leads
to maladies and death.

12:40.557 --> 12:41.897
But through a specific training,

12:42.017 --> 12:44.147
you can stop the flow
of qi entirely.

12:44.267 --> 12:46.437
It appears
that is their technique

12:46.567 --> 12:48.187
for achieving immortality.

12:48.487 --> 12:49.897
[Möge exhales]

12:50.027 --> 12:51.567
Will those techniques return you

12:51.697 --> 12:53.697
to your former health,
Boraqchin?

12:53.827 --> 12:55.197
Möge.

12:55.737 --> 12:59.157
It's just that you are supposed
to be the one sitting

12:59.287 --> 13:01.707
at the Great Kha'an's side
at Kurultais.

13:02.207 --> 13:05.127
And we desperately need
your clever mind.

13:05.247 --> 13:06.457
[BORAQCHIN] Hmm.

13:07.507 --> 13:08.717
Worry not.

13:08.837 --> 13:11.047
Kurultais aren't the only way
to decide things.

13:11.167 --> 13:12.337
[MÖGE] Huh?

13:12.467 --> 13:13.757
[BORAQCHIN]
What's most important is

13:13.887 --> 13:16.387
to discreetly maneuver
all manner of affairs.

13:16.927 --> 13:18.307
And now then,

13:18.427 --> 13:21.097
tell me about everything
you have heard lately.

13:21.937 --> 13:23.147
[Möge chuckles]

13:23.977 --> 13:25.397
[SITARA] Prince Tolui's plan

13:25.517 --> 13:27.437
puts most of the burden
on himself.

13:27.567 --> 13:28.897
But should he succeed,

13:29.027 --> 13:31.067
he will also earn
the most acclaim.

13:31.647 --> 13:34.237
I believe he will
most likely succeed.

13:34.867 --> 13:36.777
After all, the House of Tolui

13:36.907 --> 13:39.077
does have the strongest army
of the Mongols.

13:39.537 --> 13:42.787
The Mongol army typically
employs audacious tactics,

13:42.907 --> 13:44.957
which will startle the enemy.

13:45.747 --> 13:46.787
However...

13:46.917 --> 13:49.917
However,
the other Mongol princes

13:50.047 --> 13:51.757
will reach the same conclusion.

13:51.877 --> 13:53.717
The House of Tolui...

13:53.837 --> 13:55.177
[BOTH]...is too powerful.

13:55.297 --> 13:56.467
[Möge gasps]

13:56.797 --> 14:00.347
Even if Tolui doesn't intend
to betray anyone,

14:00.477 --> 14:02.767
should the Houses begin
to fear his strength,

14:02.887 --> 14:04.767
and harbor distrust
toward him...

14:05.147 --> 14:07.017
and should they decide
to collude

14:07.147 --> 14:09.107
against the House of Tolui,

14:09.397 --> 14:11.527
I am certain...

14:12.527 --> 14:14.147
[SITARA]
The Mongols will fracture.

14:14.277 --> 14:16.447
And eventually fall to ruin.

14:16.567 --> 14:17.697
[BORAQCHIN] There will be those

14:17.827 --> 14:20.287
who aim to sow
the seeds of discord.

14:20.407 --> 14:22.207
But then, what can we do?

14:22.327 --> 14:23.497
Möge...

14:23.617 --> 14:26.497
You are still young
and beautiful, unlike me.

14:26.627 --> 14:27.957
And honest and amiable.

14:28.087 --> 14:29.287
[MÖGE] Uh...

14:29.917 --> 14:32.717
[BORAQCHIN] To ensure
the Mongols are not divided,

14:32.837 --> 14:35.507
and to ensure
our hearts remain as one,

14:35.637 --> 14:38.387
I need you to take steps
in my stead.

14:38.507 --> 14:39.637
[MÖGE] Hmm.

14:40.507 --> 14:43.347
I'll do what you need
of me, Boraqchin.

14:43.477 --> 14:44.517
♪

14:46.887 --> 14:48.727
[SITARA]
Driven into a closed-off city

14:48.857 --> 14:51.687
to ultimately perish
from hunger and cold.

14:51.817 --> 14:55.027
The people of Tus
could have met the same fate.

14:55.697 --> 14:58.067
To the citizens of Kaifeng,

14:58.197 --> 15:01.447
I'd be no different
than any other Mongol.

15:02.497 --> 15:03.827
♪

15:18.847 --> 15:20.927
The Great Kha'an
heads off to war,

15:21.047 --> 15:23.597
and Prince Chagatai stays
to watch the steppe.

15:23.727 --> 15:25.767
What shall we be doing
during this time?

15:25.887 --> 15:28.307
[TÖREGENE] We will accompany
the Great Kha'an's army

15:28.437 --> 15:29.557
to the front-line camp.

15:29.687 --> 15:32.017
Chagatai is here now
to say his farewells

15:32.147 --> 15:33.107
to the Great Kha'an.

15:33.227 --> 15:34.567
Once we depart,

15:34.687 --> 15:37.527
we probably won't be seeing him
for quite a long time.

15:37.647 --> 15:40.027
[SITARA] To cause turmoil
among the Mongols,

15:40.157 --> 15:42.787
we need a faction that will
oppose the House of Tolui.

15:42.907 --> 15:45.577
The House of Chagatai is
an indispensable part of that.

15:45.707 --> 15:49.167
Well then, please allow me
to go to him as your messenger,

15:49.287 --> 15:51.587
and give Prince Chagatai
our warmest regards.

15:51.707 --> 15:54.377
I, Fatima,
am your humble servant.

15:59.717 --> 16:00.757
[QADAQ] Hmm?

16:00.887 --> 16:02.847
[cattle mooing]

16:05.807 --> 16:07.057
[hammering]

16:07.177 --> 16:09.597
[indistinct chatter]

16:15.737 --> 16:16.897
[horse neighs]

16:19.857 --> 16:22.697
Hold on. Why are you
following me, Sir Qadaq?

16:22.827 --> 16:24.657
I can't let you go by yourself.

16:24.787 --> 16:26.747
Oh, I never took you
to be such a gentleman.

16:26.867 --> 16:29.077
No, I'm saying
I don't trust you.

16:29.207 --> 16:31.877
Lady Töregene trusts me,
isn't that enough?

16:32.287 --> 16:34.627
Well, she's not the one I serve.

16:34.747 --> 16:36.337
So it's a long story.

16:36.457 --> 16:38.797
But I'm actually acting
on someone else's ord...

16:38.917 --> 16:40.217
[gasps]

16:43.427 --> 16:44.507
[gasps]

16:45.427 --> 16:46.677
[gasps]

16:49.097 --> 16:50.727
[Sitara pants]

16:52.147 --> 16:55.317
[MÖGE] Hey! Aren't you
Töregene's slave?

16:55.437 --> 16:58.027
Yes, you there.
What are you doing out here?

16:58.147 --> 16:59.777
[Sitara gasps] This woman...

16:59.897 --> 17:02.867
is Lady Möge, the fourth wife
of the Great Kha'an!

17:02.987 --> 17:07.037
Oh. I see.
You just don't learn, do you?

17:07.577 --> 17:09.407
[Sitara gasps, whimpers]

17:10.907 --> 17:12.287
Are you lost again?

17:12.417 --> 17:15.167
-Hm?
-You are lost, aren't you?

17:15.287 --> 17:17.377
I know! I bet you're
still struggling

17:17.497 --> 17:19.297
to learn the locations
of all the tents in our camp.

17:19.417 --> 17:20.667
I've had my suspicions

17:20.797 --> 17:22.717
ever since you got caught
wandering around

17:22.837 --> 17:25.887
and Töregene had to make up
an excuse for you.

17:26.007 --> 17:29.387
-Or maybe...
-Fine, you figured it out.

17:29.517 --> 17:31.387
-[cries]
-That's what I thought.

17:31.517 --> 17:32.897
-What should I do?
-Hmm.

17:33.017 --> 17:34.687
I'll bring shame
upon Lady Töregene

17:34.807 --> 17:36.437
and be scolded again.

17:36.567 --> 17:38.727
It's no business of mine
if Töregene scolds you.

17:38.857 --> 17:41.737
But bringing shame to the
Great Kha'an is another thing.

17:41.857 --> 17:43.027
Allow me to show you the way.

17:43.317 --> 17:47.117
[exclaims] Really? I can't
thank you enough, Lady Möge.

17:47.407 --> 17:49.327
I need to figure
a way out of this.

17:50.537 --> 17:53.537
Something about her
seems different than last time.

17:54.577 --> 17:56.787
-The earrings.
-[Möge gasps]

17:58.047 --> 18:00.547
Uh... I'm so sorry.

18:01.207 --> 18:04.007
Do I look odd without them?

18:04.387 --> 18:07.597
Oh, no, I wouldn't say
you look "odd."

18:08.137 --> 18:10.307
-But...
-[Möge sighs]

18:10.427 --> 18:13.437
[SITARA] Did you happen
to misplace them recently?

18:13.597 --> 18:14.807
[Möge grunts]

18:14.937 --> 18:16.017
No.

18:16.557 --> 18:18.897
The Great Kha'an chose
to sell them.

18:19.027 --> 18:20.067
[POOR MAN] Great Kha'an!

18:20.437 --> 18:23.987
Oh, Great Kha'an, I beg of you
to buy this melon from me.

18:24.107 --> 18:26.157
I am just ever so impoverished.

18:26.277 --> 18:27.777
It's so small.

18:27.907 --> 18:30.827
Möge, please give this man
those earrings you're wearing.

18:30.947 --> 18:32.037
[MÖGE] What!

18:32.537 --> 18:35.787
[poor man exclaims]

18:35.917 --> 18:38.087
[laughs]

18:38.207 --> 18:39.837
[ÖGEDEI] Worry not, Möge.

18:40.337 --> 18:42.337
I truly believe
that those earrings

18:42.457 --> 18:45.127
are destined to return
to you in the future.

18:45.677 --> 18:47.547
He said they'll return?

18:47.677 --> 18:49.097
What could he have meant
by that?

18:49.217 --> 18:50.467
I don't know in the least.

18:50.717 --> 18:53.347
I still cannot understand the
Great Kha'an in the slightest.

18:53.467 --> 18:54.847
-[CHINQAI] Lady Möge!
-Mm?

18:54.977 --> 18:57.687
Lady Möge,
the Great Kha'an calls for you.

18:57.807 --> 18:59.317
What does he want?

18:59.437 --> 19:01.187
I wasn't informed
of the details.

19:01.317 --> 19:04.187
-[exhales] Chuu!
-[horse neighs]

19:05.357 --> 19:07.067
[ÖGEDEI]
It shouldn't be long now.

19:07.197 --> 19:08.317
[hooves clopping]

19:09.577 --> 19:10.867
Oh, there she is.

19:10.987 --> 19:12.617
Greetings, Möge.

19:12.997 --> 19:14.447
Come sit here.

19:20.087 --> 19:21.667
I have here a gift for you.

19:23.337 --> 19:24.417
[Möge gasps]

19:25.877 --> 19:27.257
[MÖGE] It can't be.

19:27.377 --> 19:28.757
[Sitara gasps]

19:30.597 --> 19:32.767
[Möge exclaiming]

19:33.387 --> 19:35.307
But these are my earrings!

19:35.427 --> 19:37.227
[ÖGEDEI] Where did you manage
to obtain these?

19:37.347 --> 19:39.857
That would be Khorasan.

19:39.977 --> 19:42.687
While I was on my journey
to Samarkand,

19:42.817 --> 19:45.567
I was fortunate enough
to meet a trader who told me

19:45.687 --> 19:47.857
that he had some fine treasures
from the east.

19:47.987 --> 19:49.947
Might I interest you in these?

19:51.827 --> 19:54.287
I asked him where he ever
could have come across

19:54.407 --> 19:55.997
such magnificent pearl earrings.

19:56.117 --> 19:58.747
He said that he found them
in a Uyghur city

19:58.867 --> 20:00.707
by a random stroke of luck.

20:00.837 --> 20:01.997
-He received them...
-Please, sir.

20:02.287 --> 20:04.497
...from a poor man on the verge
of starving to death,

20:04.627 --> 20:07.257
in exchange
for a few loaves of bread.

20:07.967 --> 20:09.927
So Khorasan, huh?

20:10.047 --> 20:11.847
That's further than I expected.

20:11.967 --> 20:14.257
I believe earrings
as splendid as these

20:14.387 --> 20:16.807
truly befit the grand conqueror
of the world.

20:16.927 --> 20:18.887
That is why
I came here immediately

20:19.017 --> 20:22.267
to present them as an offering,
Great Kha'an.

20:23.227 --> 20:26.737
[MÖGE]
They really did return to me.

20:26.857 --> 20:29.147
Thank you
for delivering them to me.

20:29.277 --> 20:30.987
I will buy all of your goods,

20:31.117 --> 20:32.577
and your fellow merchants'
as well.

20:32.697 --> 20:34.737
[exclaims] Thank you very much.

20:34.867 --> 20:35.947
All of them?

20:36.077 --> 20:38.747
Bring me more of your wares
in the future.

20:38.867 --> 20:40.537
You will not regret it.

20:45.457 --> 20:46.667
[CHINQAI] Uh...

20:47.337 --> 20:49.587
Uh... Ah, over there will do.

20:49.717 --> 20:51.337
Just put them
with all the others.

20:51.467 --> 20:52.927
Be careful handling that.

20:53.047 --> 20:55.637
[TRADER 1] I didn't expect him
to buy everything from us.

20:55.757 --> 20:58.637
Coming to Mongolia
was the right decision.

20:58.767 --> 20:59.847
[SITARA] Excuse me.

20:59.977 --> 21:01.307
[TRADERS] Hmm?

21:01.437 --> 21:04.607
My apologies.
You traveled here from Khorasan?

21:04.727 --> 21:06.317
[ABD] We did. Who are you?

21:06.437 --> 21:08.897
I originally hail
from Khorasan as well.

21:09.027 --> 21:11.607
Why have you made your way
all the way to Mongolia?

21:11.737 --> 21:13.197
You're asking why?

21:13.317 --> 21:15.947
It is simple.
Because Mongolia is where

21:16.077 --> 21:18.037
the most profit
is to be had, of course.

21:18.157 --> 21:20.287
We had figured that
the Mongol emperor would be

21:20.407 --> 21:23.077
more likely than most
to offer high prices for wares

21:23.207 --> 21:25.167
coming from Khorasan
and points west.

21:25.287 --> 21:27.797
But weren't you afraid
to come here?

21:27.917 --> 21:29.917
The journey is a long one,

21:30.047 --> 21:32.297
and the Mongols
are a frightening people.

21:32.427 --> 21:35.757
Not at all. In fact, it is safer
to travel now than before.

21:35.887 --> 21:37.097
[Sitara gasps]

21:37.427 --> 21:40.387
The Mongols appoint officials to
govern the lands they conquer.

21:40.517 --> 21:43.727
Their duty is to protect
merchants passing through them.

21:43.847 --> 21:46.857
[TRADER] The emperor is
a remarkable man, indeed.

21:46.977 --> 21:49.277
[ÖGEDEI]
Thanks to your lovely earrings,

21:49.397 --> 21:52.357
I have learned that
all is functioning as it should.

21:52.487 --> 21:53.817
♪

21:58.867 --> 22:00.787
[ÖGEDEI]
I have to wonder, though.

22:01.407 --> 22:03.407
Will people come
to see it my way

22:03.537 --> 22:05.837
after we have defeated
all the Jin?

22:08.837 --> 22:11.207
[♪ closing theme song playing]

23:39.047 --> 23:42.267
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next time,
"Great Khatun Boraqchin."
